  "verification_notes": [
    "UI screenshots use declared construction supplies, standing positions and cleared or revived enemy fixtures; the separate natural journey does not.",
    "The district GUI suite operates real map buttons, clicks the visible world flag, starts and interrupts timed work, deploys G, observes a distinct enemy target, selects an outpost night role using the real dropdown, and checks four resolutions/fullscreen and unclipped detail text.",
    "Five new real processes preserve unfinished construction, complete it with one payment, restore active decoy and enemy memory, physically return, reserve crew resources, and prevent duplicate settlement.",
    "Targeted rule cases cover no-ammunition guns, double-booked ammo, heating/fuel contention, weapon wear, outdoor exposure, failed duty and fatal gear loss.",
    "Authentic schema15 fixture retains original envelope/hash and opened-route state; migration preserves stock, route and enemy records and grants no outposts or lures.",
    "A previous world-icon transform reset is fixed and verified against the actual rendered player pixel. The route intent also follows the actual selected ladder.",
    "All 60 final runtime hashes match source, clean verification copy and export inputs. Final graphical repeats cover the visual-only flag placement change.",
    "The exported acceptance additionally verifies map/role UI, timed paid construction and a saved lure with a separate enemy target at four native resolutions; normal exported game is tested separately with genuine OS input and close/restart."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Windows packages are exported using official Godot 4.6.3 templates; Windows hardware and PowerShell acceptance remain unverified.",
    "Audio audibility requires a real device.",
    "Continuous exported Linux desktop test ran two minutes, not thirty; software rendering is not a hardware performance benchmark.",
    "The unassisted new-feature journey spans two nights, not a full multi-strategy 35-day balance proof.",
    "Outpost duty and home raids are night settlements, not new real-time companion or siege scenes.",
    "Maps remain two horizontal floors; full room/door/visibility systems and varied campaign starts remain future work.",
    "These independently implemented mechanics are not a claim of matching or surpassing the overall maturity of This War of Mine."
  ]
